      "page_title": "Recursion, Templates & Pitfalls",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Head<T> = T extends",
            "  [infer H extends string, ...any[]]",
            "  ? H : never;  // TS 4.7",
            "type P<S> = S extends",
            "  `${infer A}-${infer B}`",
            "  ? [A, B] : never;",
            "type Q = P<'a-b'>; // ['a','b']"
          ],
          "note": "`infer X extends` narrows the capture"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Recursion and templates",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Unwrap<T> =",
            "  T extends Promise<infer U>",
            "    ? Unwrap<U> : T;",
            "type X = Unwrap<Promise<Promise<number>>>;",
            "// number  (own Awaited)"
          ],
          "note": "recursion peels every layer"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Input",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Head<T>`",
              "`['a', 1]`",
              "'a'"
            ],
            [
              "`Head<T>`",
              "`[1, 'a']`",
              "never"
            ],
            [
              "`Unwrap<T>`",
              "`Promise<string>`",
              "string"
            ],
            [
              "`Unwrap<T>`",
              "`number`",
              "number"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Expecting a conditional on a generic `T` inside a body to resolve; it is **deferred** until T is known",
            "`boolean` is `true | false`, so `IsString<boolean>` distributes and gives `false`, and a check like `IsTrue<boolean>` yields `true | false`",
            "Forgetting `[T]` when you want one answer for a whole union",
            "Reading `never` input as an error: it silently yields `never`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Boolean dry run",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type IsTrue<T> =",
            "  T extends true ? 1 : 0;",
            "type A = IsTrue<boolean>;",
            "// 1 | 0  (true->1, false->0)",
            "type B = [boolean] extends [true]",
            "  ? 1 : 0;  // 0"
          ],
          "note": "wrap in [] for one answer"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Check",
            "Input",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`IsTrue<T>`",
              "true",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "`IsTrue<T>`",
              "boolean",
              "1 | 0"
            ],
            [
              "`[T] extends [true]`",
              "boolean",
              "0"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type N = IsTrue<never>;",
            "// never  (nothing to distribute)",
            "type M = [never] extends [true]",
            "  ? 1 : 0;  // 1"
          ],
          "note": "wrapping makes never a real input"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Own the pattern: `infer` to read, `extends` to test",
            "Recursive unwrap needs a base case, or it never ends",
            "Test each type on a union, a `never` and a plain value"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "Naked `T` distributes; `[T]` checks the whole union once."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Debug tip",
          "text": "Hover a type alias with a concrete input to see what the conditional resolved to."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "typescript",
      "subtitle": "types that branch"
