      "page_title": "Utility Types: Reshape & Select",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What They Are",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Utility types== are generic aliases that ship with TypeScript. Each one is a small {blue:mapped} or {blue:conditional} type you would otherwise write by hand.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Reshape an Object",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Effect",
            "Gotcha"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Partial<T>`",
              "every key gets ?",
              "update payloads"
            ],
            [
              "`Required<T>`",
              "-? strips ?",
              "opposite of Partial"
            ],
            [
              "`Readonly<T>`",
              "adds readonly",
              "**shallow**, compile-time only"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Partial<T> = {",
            "  [K in keyof T]?: T[K]",
            "};",
            "type Req<T> = {",
            "  [K in keyof T]-?: T[K]",
            "};"
          ],
          "note": "Required is Partial with -?"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Choose Keys",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Pick<T, K extends keyof T>` keeps only the listed keys",
            "`Omit<T, K extends keyof any>` drops keys",
            "==Omit== never checks K against T's keys, so typos pass",
            "`Record<K, V>` builds an object from a key union"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type P = Pick<User, 'id' | 'name'>;",
            "type O = Omit<User, 'email'>;",
            "type R = Record<'a' | 'b', number>;",
            "// Omit<T,K> = Pick<T,",
            "//   Exclude<keyof T, K>>"
          ],
          "note": "Omit<User,'emial'> compiles silently"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Filter and Extract",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Input",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Exclude<U, X>`",
              "'a'|'b', 'a'",
              "'b'"
            ],
            [
              "`Extract<U, X>`",
              "'a'|'b', 'a'",
              "'a'"
            ],
            [
              "`NonNullable<T>`",
              "string|null",
              "string"
            ],
            [
              "`ReturnType<F>`",
              "() => number",
              "number"
            ],
            [
              "`Parameters<F>`",
              "(a: string) => void",
              "[a: string]"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Combine them",
          "text": "`Partial<Pick<User, 'name'>>` makes a single optional field for a patch."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type DOmit<T, K extends",
            "  keyof any> = T extends unknown",
            "  ? Omit<T, K> : never;"
          ],
          "note": "naked T makes it distribute"
        }
      ],
