    {
      "page_title": "Pitfalls and Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mistakes to Avoid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**Over-generic**: five type params nobody can read; prefer ==overloads==",
            "**Unnecessary**: `log<T>(x: T): void` equals `(x: unknown) => void`",
            "**Used once**: lint `no-unnecessary-type-parameters` flags it",
            "**Cast inside**: `return {} as T` hides a bug; value may not satisfy T",
            "**Runtime T**: no `new T()` or `typeof T`; pass a constructor or tag"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "// T appears once: useless",
            "function log<T>(x: T): void {}",
            "// same, and honest:",
            "const log = (x: unknown) => {};",
            "// bug hidden by the cast",
            "function mk<T>(): T { return {} as T; }"
          ],
          "note": "a cast silences the compiler, not the bug"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Recursion and Cost",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deep recursion: ==excessively deep and possibly infinite== at ~50 levels",
            "Tail-recursive conditional types stretch the limit to ~1000",
            "Heavy conditional and mapped types slow `tsc` and the editor",
            "Measure with `tsc --generateTrace dir`, then read the trace",
            "Unreadable errors: wrap with `Simplify<T> = { [K in keyof T]: T[K] } & {}`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Pick the Right Tool",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Choice",
            "Wins at",
            "Costs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Overloads",
              "clean per-case signatures",
              "more lines to write"
            ],
            [
              "Generic + conditional",
              "one signature",
              "weaker body check"
            ],
            [
              "`unknown`",
              "values only passed around",
              "output type is lost"
            ],
            [
              "Generic `<T>`",
              "output depends on input",
              "harder to read"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "If T never links input to output, use `unknown`. If one signature needs a conditional, try overloads first."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Runtime Boundaries",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Object.keys` returns `string[]`, not `(keyof T)[]`",
            "`Object.entries` and `JSON.parse` lose generics too",
            "Cast at ==one small boundary==, not all over the code",
            "Types vanish at runtime: pass a ==tag value== when you need one"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function make<T>(C: new () => T): T {",
            "  return new C(); // not new T()",
            "}",
            "const d = make(Date); // Date",
            "const keys = Object.keys(o) as",
            "  (keyof typeof o)[]; // one cast"
          ],
          "note": "pass the constructor, never T itself"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Tools for type tests",
          "text": "Use `expectTypeOf` (vitest) or `tsd`. Both fail the build when a type drifts."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "typescript",
      "subtitle": "Trade-offs in generics"
